Z||000004||David Gamache||01-05-2000||10:38 PM||||The aftermarket pannels eventually come loose and fall off the vehicle. I eventually made my own that required a sealer and four capped screws to keep the pannels in place. But making a set of pannels is not for everyone. Best to use factory replacements.||||reg||1
Z||000005||TOM||01-06-2000||01:39 AM||||I know someone who sells them. Please contact me for details||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dan87GT||01-06-2000||12:30 PM||||David, are you saying that that factory panels are bolted on and the FieroHeaven ones are only double-sided tape?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phil||01-06-2000||01:46 PM||||Factory uses double face tape. After I had my 88 painted I used 3M tape on the one window that wasn't cracked and it has been fine for over a year. It sounds like either the wrong tape was used or the surfaces weren't clean. It shouldn't fall off. On the newer cars a lot of the trim is attached with tape.||||reg||1
Z||000008||David Gamache||01-07-2000||01:13 AM||||The aftermarket pannels have a painted inner surface to which the double sided tape is attached. Eventually the paint lifts and the tape fails allowing the pannels to come off. The Fiero store can confirm this problem and they no longer carry them. (The screw and cap design to which I refered was part of a design for pannels I made not pruchased)||||reg||1
Z||000009||william_thorniii||01-09-2000||03:13 AM||||I used to work for an automotive body side molding supplier.  Our moldings that were taped on had to withstand over 200 lbf before experiencing adhesion failure.  Naturally they were on factory doors at that point so paint quality is an issue.  So is surface preparation.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000010||Phil||01-09-2000||10:17 AM||||Didn't know about the paint thing  looks like I'm gonna find out soon.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Cooter||01-09-2000||10:45 AM||||When I put in the scooped replacement windows, I just ran a bead of urethane around it. I did this because the tape was too thin to fill in the surface irregularities between the panel and the body. I don't think the panels are going anywhere. I just hope that they never have to be removed!||||reg||1
Z||000012||johnmac||01-14-2000||06:21 AM||||I have tried to placed an order with Fiero Heaven. No responses to emails. I tried calling them but phone is disconnected. Are they out of business?<P>Who supplies the best quality GT Quarterwindows? Please email at johnmac@mpinet.net<P>Note: I have used 3M 5200 on my boat projects and it will "never" come off!<P>John||||reg||1
